[hawthorn@wam.umd.edu (Ian James Hawthorn) writes:]
[] A Suggestion: It seems to me that every nasty item in nethack should have 
[] some sort of use. Nasty scrolls and potions for example can be rewritten or
[] converted to holy water. There are a number of items however which seem to
[] have a downside but no upside. It seems to me that finding a useful
[] purpose for these nasty things would greatly improve the game.
[]
[] The following examples are the kind of thing that I mean.
[]
[] #1: Rings of hunger.

cursed - make you hungry quick, can't be removed.
uncursed - can be removed but otherwise the same
blessed - improves odds against choking {gluttony is still punishable!}
          and perhaps acts like the old (rogue) ring of slow digestion.

[] #2: Loadstones

when dropped always becomes re-cursed, that's its magic ...
cursed - can be picked up and becomes extra heavy, can't be dropped/thrown.
uncursed - normal weight, can be dropped/thrown as a stone.
blessed - has negative weight, forces levitation if you're not carrying
          enough (you'd have to drop the stone to get down, oh no it's
          cursed again ...).

[] #3: Amulets of strangulation

cursed - can't be removed, strangles ...
uncursed - can be removed
blessed - strangulation resistance ... however walking into pools could
          still be a problem as your armor and weapons may rust with
          each move and your scrolls could dissolve and your potions
          float away and your wands may get waterlogged, again with
          a random chance each move.

[] #4: A cursed -5 ring of adornment, etc. ...

i'm not comfortable with the reversing enchantment scheme.

here's an oppurtunity to knock a stupid of mine:

certain rings should have a cumulative effect (without regard to
suggestions made above) as in:

ring of invisibility: reverses your invisible state (two rings would
      negate each other).

ring of hunger: affects your hunger rate, that is one ring makes you
      twice as hungry but two rings make you half as hungry in a given
      period of time.

ring of teleportation: enhances your teleportation skills.  if you're
      jumpy it's teleport control, if you're not then you can teleport.
      elimnates (teleport control ring).

ring of polymorph: one ring may polymorph you in time. two rings gives
      you polymorph control (again eliminating a ring).

ring of aggravation: reverses your aggravation stat.

ring of levitation: reverses your levitation stat.

ring of fire:
ring of cold:
ring of shock:
ring of poison: reverse the appropriate resistance (i.e. wearing a
    ring of poison as a normal barbarian would be a mistake).

and so on ...

under this scheme gloves of fumbling would negate boots of stumbling.

a ring of water would cancel boots of water walking but would provide
    water walking if worn alone.

a ring of disintegration would provide resistance if you weren't
    already but would attempt to kill you (after a random time) if
    you were!

to my warped mind this makes rings more powerful and strengthens game
    balance while making ring identification more important and
    interestingly problematic (do i drop this ring down the drain?).

